Below is the change description:
The original documentation did not explain how to access transport-specific metadata (such as HTTP headers) within tools. Because the MCP server is designed to be transport-agnostic, providing this guide allows developers to integrate context-sensitive data, like authentication tokens, while maintaining the intended architecture.
Added a new section to the MCP Server Boot Starter documentation titled 'Adding data to McpTransportContext', which provides code examples for configuring a 'TransportContextExtractor' and accessing metadata within tool methods using 'McpSyncRequestContext'.

